Chapter: ShadowBuiltin

 Measured 2026-07-18, and worth knowing before trusting either
 behaviour: the definition does NOT always win. Shadowing abs, int-mod,
 text-contains and is-digit substitutes the definition; shadowing
 text-length does not, and the builtin answers. The likely reason is
 that a builtin lowered to its own IR node never reaches the
 emit-builtin dispatch a definition can displace. So the hazard is
 inconsistent rather than uniform, which is the worse shape: the same
 shadowing pattern behaves differently per builtin and the source gives
 no clue which. That is the argument for warning at the definition site
 rather than reasoning about it at each call.

  abs : Integer -> Integer
  abs (n) = 94

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("abs(-4) = " & show (abs (0 - 4)))
  end
